# The root *.js set is exactly the SOURCES list in build/package-extension.sh —
# tests, build helpers and install-extras all live in subdirectories, so a glob
# cannot pick them up. One glob instead of a second hand-maintained
# copy of that list; if the two ever diverge the packager already fails loudly
# on a missing source.
*.js                                   usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/wallpaper-suite@spencercnorton.github.io/
metadata.json                          usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/wallpaper-suite@spencercnorton.github.io/
debian/generated/build-info.json       usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/wallpaper-suite@spencercnorton.github.io/
icons/wallpaper-suite.svg              usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/wallpaper-suite@spencercnorton.github.io/icons/

# Distro convention, and load-bearing: nothing packaged may ship a
# gschemas.compiled, so the extension directory deliberately gets NO schemas/
# subdirectory. Extension.getSettings() only builds a private schema source
# when that directory exists; without it the lookup falls through to the
# default source, which is where dh_installgsettings' trigger compiles this.
# Shipping schemas/ with the XML alone would make new_from_directory() fail.
schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.wallpaper-suite.gschema.xml usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/

install-extras/wallpaper-suitectl      usr/bin/
install-extras/wallpaper-suite         usr/bin/
install-extras/launcher/*.js           usr/share/wallpaper-suite/launcher/
install-extras/wallpaper-suite-migrate.desktop etc/xdg/autostart/
install-extras/wallpaper-suite.desktop usr/share/applications/
install-extras/wallpaper-suite.svg     usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/
